        <h1>AI Tools Transforming Education</h1>
        <p><time datetime="2026-09-14">September 14, 2026</time></p>
      </header>

      <figure>
        <img src="https://share.google/jwmbywqUYiF0GWMc0" 
             alt="Students using laptops with AI-powered learning tools" 
             width="600" height="300">
        <figcaption>AI-powered platforms are reshaping classrooms worldwide.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section id="background">
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>
          Artificial Intelligence (<abbr title="Artificial Intelligence">AI</abbr>) has steadily 
          integrated into classrooms, offering personalized learning experiences. 
          Teachers now use AI-driven dashboards to track progress, while students 
          benefit from adaptive quizzes that highlight <mark>areas needing improvement</mark>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="analysis">
        <h2>Analysis</h2>
        <p>
          Experts argue that AI can reduce administrative burdens and allow educators 
          to focus more on mentoring. However, ethical concerns remain, especially 
          regarding data privacy. For example, some platforms rely on algorithms 
          written in <code>JavaScript</code> to process student interactions, raising 
          questions about transparency and accountability.
        </p>
      </section>

      <blockquote>
        <p>"AI in education is not about replacing teachers, but empowering them."</p>
        <footer>— <cite>Dr. Maria Lopez, Educational Technologist</cite></footer>
      </blockquote>

      <aside>
        <h2>Key Facts</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>AI adoption in schools grew 35% in 2025.</li>
          <li>Top uses: grading automation, adaptive learning, language translation.</li>
          <li>Concerns: privacy, bias, and equitable access.</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>

